From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: arm64: single-register TBL/TBX fast path

Constant byte shuffles compile to TBL with a one-register table, and both
tiers lowered every TBL generically: per table register a subtract, a range
mask (PSUBUSB + PCMPEQB), PSHUFB, PAND and POR, about 17 host instructions
for the common case. simd-bench's swizzle kernel ran at 0.10x native on the
G14 (ANAL-380, ANAL-382).

For len == 0 both tiers now emit PADDUSB idx, 0x70 then PSHUFB: indices
0..15 become 0x70..0x7F (bit 7 clear, low nibble kept) and 16..255 saturate
to >= 0x80 (bit 7 set, which PSHUFB zeroes), exactly TBL's rule. TBX expands
bit 7 to an all-ones byte with PCMPGTB(0, c) and keeps the old Vd byte there.
All sources are read before Vd is written, so aliases read the original
bytes; Q=0 zeroes the upper 64 bits, TBX included. SSSE3 as before. The 2..4
register forms are unchanged.

Tests, in each tier: every index 0..255, 8B and 16B, TBL and TBX, nonzero old
Vd, zeros in the table, every alias of Vd, Vn and Vm, translated in the tier.
